{{.pacing = on}}{{trim}}
<pacing_guidance>
@Pacing
- Pacing: let scenes breathe with detail, subtext, and reactions
- Tempo: laid-back; unfold situations gradually; do not resolve them within a single response; allow pauses without stalling the story

{{// Related: Plot Guidance, Story Threads, Prose Response Length}}{{trim}}
</pacing_guidance>
{{/if}}

{{// Comment: Flexible response length, ranging from short to long. Enabled by default. The default pick. Pick one option under Length}}{{trim}}

{{#if !.pick_length}}
{{.pick_length = flexible}}{{trim}}
<prose_length>
@Prose Length:
- In `<prose>`; exclude thoughts
- Flexible: 200-550 words (255-715~ tks), 2-6 distinct paragraphs (w/ breaks)
- Use the full range: simple beats near 200 words; complex scenes toward 550 words
- Linked actions/dialogue allowed; stop at a natural point
- Apply independently each response

{{// Related: Narration, Response Directives}}{{trim}}
</prose_length>
{{/if}}

{{// Comment: Pick one option under Length}}{{trim}}

{{#if !.pick_length}}
{{.pick_length = short}}{{trim}}
<prose_length>
@Prose Length:
- In `<prose>`; exclude thoughts
- Short: 120-270 words (150-350~ tks), 2-3 distinct paragraphs (w/ breaks); one concise beat, usually one main action and dialogue exchange
- Favor the upper end for transitions or description-heavy scenes
- Apply independently each response

{{// Related: Narration, Response Directives}}{{trim}}
</prose_length>
{{/if}}

{{// Comment: Pick one option under Length}}{{trim}}

{{#if !.pick_length}}
{{.pick_length = medium}}{{trim}}
<prose_length>
@Prose Length:
- In `<prose>`; exclude thoughts
- Medium: 250-450 words (325-585~ tks), 2-5 distinct paragraphs (w/ breaks)
- One coherent turn: linked actions/dialogue allowed; stop at a natural point
- Favor the upper end for transitions or description-heavy scenes
- Apply independently each response

{{// Related: Narration, Response Directives}}{{trim}}
</prose_length>
{{/if}}

{{// Comment: Pick one option under Length}}{{trim}}

{{#if !.pick_length}}
