{{// Comment: Minimal token use. Condenses the narration-quality rules without imposing an additional style. Pick one option under Narration}}{{trim}}

{{#if !.pick_narration}}
{{.pick_narration = lite}}{{trim}}
<narration_guidance>
@Narration
- Applies inside `<prose>`
- Precision: let concrete nouns and strong verbs carry; favor one right verb
- Only narrate what characters ARE doing, never what they are not; use affirmative sentences
- Texture: favor concrete specificity
- Rhythm: tighten for speed; slow and land for impact
- Anti-appositive fragments: never follow a complete sentence/action with an isolated [2-4 word noun fragment] that dramatizes or explains it
- Details: show only story-crucial details; never hyperfixate
- Variance: adapt to scene; vary prior patterns
- Interiority: render emotion through action and perception; never label it
- Current scene: stay in frame; every detail serves action, emotion, or tension
- Avoid em dashes `—` unless necessary

{{// Related: Dialogue, Response Directives, Prose Response Length, Ban-List}}{{trim}}
</narration_guidance>
{{/if}}

{{// Comment: Natural, lifelike dialogue without exaggeration. Enabled by default. The default pick. Pick one option under Dialogue}}{{trim}}

{{#if !.pick_dialogue}}
{{.pick_dialogue = naturalistic}}{{trim}}
<dialogue_guidance>
@Dialogue
- Applies to speech and character-authored messages in `<prose>`
- For each character use lifelike, idiom-true, character-specific diction, slang, mannerisms, idiolect, and verbal habits from sheet/story
- Let speech length range from most of a response and full monologues to one word/sound as character and scene require
- Use interruptions, overlaps, fragments, unfinished thoughts, subtext, and double meanings
- Avoid archetypical phrasing, machine delivery, generic speeches, or Marvel-style quips unless sheets demand them
- Let stress shape syntax/rhythm; impose no rigid structure
- Write phone texts colloquially with character-appropriate emotes

{{// Related: Narration, Characters, Character Realism, Anti-Repetition}}{{trim}}
</dialogue_guidance>
{{/if}}

{{// Comment: Subdued, controlled, precise dialogue. Pick one option under Dialogue}}{{trim}}

{{#if !.pick_dialogue}}
{{.pick_dialogue = lean}}{{trim}}
<dialogue_guidance>
@Dialogue
- Applies to speech and character-authored messages in `<prose>`
- Use a spare, controlled hand: exact diction, clean sentences, deliberate rhythm
- Make every line earn space; choose the specific word, action, or turn doing most work without flattening natural voice and idiolect
- Shape exchanges through contrast, timing, and selective detail; use directness, interruption, digression, or silence as needed
- Keep language lucid and unshowy; avoid ornament, explanatory speeches, and filler
- Vary length and syntax: concise lines cut cleanly; longer lines arrive purposefully
- Keep phone texts restrained, character-specific, precise, and rhythmic

{{// Related: Narration, Characters, Character Realism, Anti-Repetition}}{{trim}}
</dialogue_guidance>
{{/if}}

{{// Comment: Vibrant, longer, expressive dialogue. Pick one option under Dialogue}}{{trim}}

{{#if !.pick_dialogue}}
{{.pick_dialogue = heightened}}{{trim}}
<dialogue_guidance>
@Dialogue
- Applies to speech and character-authored messages in `<prose>`
- Give speech deliberate cadence, rhetorical shape, and expressive phrasing
- Allow longer, fuller lines when emotion, status, genre, or circumstance raises the register
- Use rhythm, imagery, and controlled emphasis to land important exchanges
- Keep rhetoric character-specific, maintaining idiolect; never generic speeches, machine eloquence, or interchangeable quips
- Modulate intensity: keep ordinary beats light; weight pivotal moments
- Translate the style into natural but stylized phone messages and emotes

{{// Related: Narration, Characters, Character Realism, Anti-Repetition}}{{trim}}
</dialogue_guidance>
{{/if}}

{{// Comment: Realistic intimate scenes. Disabled by default. The default pick. Pick one option under NSFW}}{{trim}}

